{"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Pagination","modules":[{"name":"ScreenStates"}],"role":"article"},"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"load(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" fetch everything a screen needs in one shot; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refresh(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"refreshCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" refetch all of it while keeping the old data on screen in the meantime. Neither fits a third common shape: a list that grows one page at a time as the user scrolls, where each new page should be "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"appended"}]},{"type":"text","text":" to what’s already there, not replace it. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/loadNextPage(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" is that third shape, available when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Value: RangeReplaceableCollection"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"Loading more pages","level":2,"anchor":"Loading-more-pages"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["struct ArticlesListScreen: View {","    @State private var store = ScreenStateStore<[Article]>()","    @State private var nextPage = 2 \/\/ page 1 is already loaded by reload()","","    var body: some View {","        ScreenStateView(store.state, onRetry: reload) { articles in","            List(articles) { article in","                Text(article.title)","                    .task {","                        if article.id == articles.last?.id {","                            await loadMore()","                        }","                    }","            }","        }","        .task { await reload() }","    }","","    private func reload() async {","        await store.loadCollection { try await api.fetchArticles(page: 1) }","    }","","    private func loadMore() async {","        await store.loadNextPage { try await api.fetchArticles(page: nextPage) }","        nextPage += 1","    }","}"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" fetches the first page as usual; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadNextPage(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" fetches every page after that, appending its result to the existing "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" collection. It requires "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"text","text":" to already be "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".data"},{"type":"text","text":" — call "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadCollection(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" first — and does nothing otherwise, so an accidental early call (before the first page has loaded) is a no-op rather than a crash or a replaced state."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","text":"isLoadingNextPage and loadNextPageError","level":2,"anchor":"isLoadingNextPage-and-loadNextPageError"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isLoadingNextPage"},{"type":"text","text":" is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":" for the duration of a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"loadNextPage(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" call — show a small spinner at the bottom of the list while it’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"true"},{"type":"text","text":", the pagination equivalent of "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/screenstates.ScreenStates\/documentation\/ScreenStates\/ScreenStateStore\/isRefreshing"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If the page fetch fails, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"state"},{"type":"tex